{"ranking": ["M10", "M11", "M8"], "fault": "M10's gate is wired to c1 instead of its own drain s1, so it is not diode-connected as the reference of the bottom NMOS cascode mirror (M10/M11). With no gate bias, M10 and M11 are off, which starves the M8/M9 cascode branch. The folded node c1 is pulled low, M6 and M7 lose their current, f1 and the tail node collapse toward ground, and M1, M2 and M5 go into triode. This explains the near-zero gain, the collapsed output swing, and the off-state of M6 through M10."}
